# OpenHamShack controller pads (shack_pad), from the OpenHamShack box's
# 91-openhamshack-pad.rules. Only group shack-input can read them: on the
# controller that is the shack-input host service, never an app
# (CONTROLLER-PAD.md §6.1). On a Linux desktop, add the operator to
# shack-input instead.
#
# Ajazz AKP03E: its hidraw nodes (input0 is the pad; input1, its keyboard
# face, is given too but never opened as the pad).
KERNEL=="hidraw*", ATTRS{idVendor}=="0300", ATTRS{idProduct}=="3002", MODE="0660", GROUP="shack-input"
# A USB keypad or keyboard the operator chose (and only that: shack-keypad
# checks the chosen list). libinput is told to leave it alone, so its keys
# never type into the screen as well; the host grabs it besides. Takes
# effect when it is next plugged in.
SUBSYSTEM=="input", KERNEL=="event*", ACTION!="remove", PROGRAM="/usr/local/sbin/shack-keypad %k", MODE="0660", GROUP="shack-input", ENV{LIBINPUT_IGNORE_DEVICE}="1"
